<title>POLAND: Poland bans imports of pigs, pork from Netherlands.</title>
<headline>Poland bans imports of pigs, pork from Netherlands.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland banned imports of pigs and unprocessed pork from the Netherlands on Friday after an outbreak of swine fever there, PAP news agency quoted the agriculture ministry as saying.</p>
<p>Bogdan Twardowski, a deputy director at the ministry veterinary department, told PAP the decision had been taken to protect the Polish market against the disease, which had not been reported in Poland since 1994.</p>
<p>Agriculture Ministry officials were not immediately available for comment on how long the ban would last.</p>
<p>Poland imported 50,000 tonnes of pork last year, but PAP said there were no available statistics on how much of this was bought from the Netherlands.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
